{"When buffer.assigned_shards is empty (e.g., during partition rebalancing), self.num_processes becomes 0, causing a ZeroDivisionError on line 65 when computing i % self.num_processes": 0.8944065570831299, "The restart threshold check uses > before incrementing, which allows MAX_PROCESS_RESTARTS + 1 total restarts instead of the intended cap, prolonging crash-loop thrashing": 0.4204668700695038, "The backpressure logic rejects ALL ingestion when ANY single process exceeds the threshold, creating global throttling from a single shard-group hotspot and potentially over-throttling the system": 0.9190080165863037, "Killed processes are not properly joined/closed before replacement, risking resource leaks in long-running deployments with frequent restarts": 0.6920700073242188, "Using comma-joined shard lists as metric tags introduces unbounded cardinality that scales with partition topology changes, creating observability cost and complexity problems": 0.6685930490493774}